      "description": "Watch Al Faisaly FC vs Al Fateh highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 26, 2026. Al Faisaly FC and Al Fateh faced off in a highly anticipated Pro League fixture on August 26, 2026 . Fans gathered to witness a contest where tactical discipline and individual brilliance were expected to take center stage. Clinical Finishing in the First Half The match began with high energy and early physical duels, resulting in a yellow card for Theo Bongonda in the 23rd minute. The deadlock was broken in the 29th minute when Lukas Haraslin found the back of the net, capitalizing on a well-placed assist from Zaydou Youssouf . The momentum continued to swing in favor of the clinical side, despite yellow cards being shown to Kennedy Boateng and Abdoulaye Seck as the battle intensified. In the 41st minute, the lead was doubled. Alexandre Mendy turned provider, setting up Christian Bassogog for a composed finish that put his side firmly in control. Just before the halftime whistle, the atmosphere grew even more heated when Eid Al-Muwallad received his first caution of the match in stoppage time. Discipline and Late Drama The second half was defined by a major shift in momentum. In the 58th minute, the referee brandished a red card to Eid Al-Muwallad , sparking heavy protests from teammates and changing the tactical landscape of the game. Playing with a numerical advantage, the leading side focused on game management, while several substitutions were made to inject fresh legs. Managers introduced players like Mohammed Jahfali , Sorriso , and Fahad Aqeel Al-Zubaidi to navigate the closing stages. Sattam Al Tumbukti also entered the referee's book late in the game. Despite the chaotic nature of the final minutes and a flurry of substitutions in the 87th minute, including Saad Al-Shurafa , the early damage proved decisive as the match concluded with a clear victory."
